Dear Cosmas,

We write further to our message sent on 2 March 2025 (the “*Response*”), in relation to your data subject rights request. We apologise for the delay in sending you our Response, which was the result of an escalation error. We address each of your concerns below.

*(1) List of personal data processed*

As noted in our Response, we have already shared with you a comprehensive copy of your personal data to which you are entitled, which is in a structured, commonly used, and machine-readable format. The folders and sub-folders into which you data has been saved are labelled according to relevant categories, but in any case please find a breakdown of the categories below:

* Acceptance rate;
* Account and profile data (including account summary, profile pictures; change logs, compliance documents, change logs, devices information and information on scheduled rides);
* Average rating, as well as a filtered breakdown of individual ratings and comments provided by passengers about you;
* Billing information (including invoices, balance reports and tax reports);
* Blocking data;
* Car application details;
* Communications data (including recent communications with passengers, emails, transcripts of conversations with Bolt Customer Support; and audio recordings of calls with Bolt Customer Support);
* Records of consents;
* Dispatch preferences;
* Geolocation / speed data;
* Verification history (including pictures provided during the verification process);
* Online status history (including online time and state logs);
* Ride history;
* Security information (including login sessions and password reset requests);
* Correspondence with TfL regarding passenger complaints issued against you; and
* Selected car history.

For further information on the categories of personal data that we process about our users, we refer you to our privacy notice available at [https://bolt.eu/en-gb/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/en-gb/privacy/privacy-for-drivers/?category=rides] .

*(2) Withheld data*

As noted in our Response, the right of access under data protection law does not provide an individual with an absolute right of full access to any and all documents containing their personal data. In particular, we have been unable to provide the following information, which has been redacted from the copies provided to you with our Response:

* Personal data of Bolt employees contained in transcripts of conversations you had with our Customer Support Team;
* Personal data of other Bolt passengers contained in transcripts of your conversations with passengers and your order history;
* Details linking a specific rating / comment provided by a passenger to a specific trip, including its date and time; and
* Details of the context and nature of any complaints made by passengers against that have been communicated to TfL;

as disclosure of such information would violate the rights and freedoms of the relevant Bolt employees and passengers, in accordance with Article 15(4) of the UK GDPR.

*(3) Information on automated processing*

Please also note that Bolt may process your personal data for the purpose of fraud detection and prevention. However, these checks do not involve automated decision-making. This is because for some checks there is always a human component involved, whereas checks that are fully automated do not produce legal or similar effects for drivers.

We hope that this addresses your concerns. If you have any additional questions or concerns, please let us know so that we can work with you to resolve them.

Yours sincerely,

*Bolt*

