*Proposed setup:*
For safety incidents where the provider is the reported (accused) party, we will hide the following fields from the [Global Event Assessment Tool|https://www.cognitoforms.com/Taxify1/globaleventassessmenttool2] in the {{Investigation}} section:

* {{Occurrence}}
* {{Demerit Decay}}
* {{Deviant Action}}
* {{Reasoning for Deviant Action}}
* We will also hide the prompt to suspend the provider account temporarily until the investigation is completed:
** {{PLACE INVESTIGATIVE SUSPENSION ON ACCUSED PARTY}}
** {{CONFIRM ANY PROVIDER'S BLOCK WITH OPS}}

As a result, the {{Action Required}} and {{Please Confirm That You Have Taken Action According to the Tool's Suggestion}} fields will also not be shown.


This ensures that CS agents who are receiving the report from the eater/courier can investigate the provider-related safety incident with related parties and log the report in the tool, but:

* they won’t be asked to fill out information which they do not have access to view ({{Occurrences}} - number of previous safety reports of the provider)
* they won’t be asked to implement temporary account suspensions to limit the provider from conducting further harm until the investigation is completed and fault, or no fault has been determined (such as provider account suspensions)
* they won’t be asked to implement consequential corrective actions (such as provider account terminations)
** _Example: this means that if a provider’s employee were to physically assault a courier-partner, the safety tool no longer proposes the CS team to suspend the provider’s account due to access limitations in Admin._
